# Add armored OpenPGP public keys that are trusted to sign release tags.
#
# This file is intentionally committed to the repository instead of stored in a
# GitLab CI variable. A tag release must be an annotated tag signed by one of
# the keys imported from this file.
#
# Example:
#
# -----BEGIN PGP PUBLIC KEY BLOCK-----
# ...
# -----END PGP PUBLIC KEY BLOCK-----
# 
# gpg --export-options export-minimal --armor --export <KEYID> >> ./trusted-release-gpg-keys.asc
#
